WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:05.569
Who can forget the endless hype for Prometheus?

00:00:05.569 --> 00:00:11.139
It was supposed to be Ridley’s Scott grand
return to the franchise that began his career:

00:00:11.139 --> 00:00:12.139
Alien.

00:00:12.139 --> 00:00:16.670
Here he would resurrect the franchise from
the pits of those Alien vs Predator films.

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:20.770
And answer all those pestering fan’s questions
like, where did the Alien really come from

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:23.290
and who was that dead giant space jockey?

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:26.750
Plus, with an all star cast, how could the
film fail?

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:29.950
It was a sure thing, destined to spawn a new
franchise.

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:33.079
And yet... people were really disappointed.

00:00:33.079 --> 00:00:38.250
So much so that when the sequel, Alien Covenant
was released, barely anyone showed up, effectively

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:41.070
killing this “sure-to-be” franchise.

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:46.250
Most people criticize these prequels for two
MAJOR reasons.One, all the unimaginably stupid

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:50.980
decisions the human characters make, which:
"Charlie, don't be an idiot."

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:53.309
"She is beautiful."

00:00:53.309 --> 00:00:55.840
Yeah, there are quite a lot of.

00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:00.239
And Two, because Prometheus and Alien: Covenant
raise a lot of lofty questions: "Where do

00:01:00.239 --> 00:01:01.440
we come from?

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:03.790
What is our purpose?

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:05.009
What happens when we die?"

00:01:05.009 --> 00:01:09.479
But then never bothers to answer them or,
to be honest, really even tried to.

00:01:09.479 --> 00:01:13.350
So it seems like they’re just pseudo-intellectual
nonsense-- as if just by raising a couple

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:18.149
Philosophy 101 questions, somehow the films
will become inherently deep.

00:01:18.149 --> 00:01:19.649
But is that really the case?

00:01:19.649 --> 00:01:25.159
Let’s find out in this WE on Prometheus
&amp; Alien: Covenant: Deep or Dumb?

00:01:25.159 --> 00:01:27.139
And yep, spoilers ahead.

00:01:27.139 --> 00:01:30.499
Before we get started, a question we keep
getting asked is, whatever happened to Earthling

00:01:30.499 --> 00:01:31.499
Cinema.

00:01:31.499 --> 00:01:33.899
Well guys, it's still around it's just on
a new channel.

00:01:33.899 --> 00:01:38.179
If you're not familiar, Earthling Cinema's
a Wisecrack show where a smart-ass alien from

00:01:38.179 --> 00:01:42.529
the future analyses the culture of a long
destroyed earth, mostly it's movies.

00:01:42.529 --> 00:01:46.789
Well it's moved to it's own channel and we've
renamed it Alien's Guide since it's about

00:01:46.789 --> 00:01:48.469
so much more than cinema now.

00:01:48.469 --> 00:01:53.189
In addition to tackling films like Captain
America Civil War and Sharknado, Garyx is

00:01:53.189 --> 00:01:57.779
branching out into television, anime, and
a new sub-series called Earthling Culture

00:01:57.779 --> 00:02:00.270
where he dives into things like Disneyland.

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:03.849
I've always loved this show and I feel like
it's gotten even better since we launched

00:02:03.849 --> 00:02:07.489
the new channel, so you're not gonna want
to miss the new episodes we got coming out

00:02:07.489 --> 00:02:08.489
soon.

00:02:08.489 --> 00:02:11.810
Garyx is gonna cover something that people
have requested a lot, The Office, and he's

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:13.970
got a lot to say about the paper business.

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:18.450
There's a link below to subscribe, so be sure
to check it out, and now, back to the show.

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:22.890
Alright guys, let's get started with a recap:
Prometheus begins in the early 21st century

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:27.440
as a group of humans, plus one android obsessed
with Lawrence of Arabia, travel to a distant

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:31.380
planet in search of their makers, an alien
race known as the Engineers.

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:35.570
However, when our motley crew of space travelers
reach the planet, they discover a strange

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:38.350
military base used to create bio-weapons.

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:42.250
The crew get exposed to some of the black
gooey stuff and turn on one another.

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:47.880
Meanwhile that Peter O ’Toole looking android,
David, discovers one of the Engineers in cryo-sleep.

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:51.480
Turns out the Engineers were none too happy
with their creation and were actually planning

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:54.900
to release the black goo on Earth to wipe
us all out.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:58.290
"Sometimes to create, one must first destroy."

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:03.480
When David wakes the Engineer up, he tries
to do just that, prompting Idris Elba to sacrifice

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:08.800
himself, leaving our final girl, Shaw, on
a mission to discover just why humanity’s

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.230
creators were so keen on pulling the plug.

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:15.780
Yet by the time Alien: Covenant comes around,
Shaw’s already dead, and David has wiped

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:21.010
out the Engineer’s planet, using the black
goo to create, you guessed it, the Alien.

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:25.010
And yeah, that’s pretty much all that happens
in the entire two-hour sequel -- and it mostly

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:26.490
happens off-screen.

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:28.490
So what’s actually going on in these films?

00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:33.830
An early flashback to Shaw’s childhood,
begins to tease out the answer: "Why did he

00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:34.830
die?

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:36.340
Cause sooner or later everyone does.

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:39.010
Where do they go?

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:46.700
Everyone has their own word, heaven, paradise.

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:48.880
Whatever it's called, it's someplace beautiful.

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:51.050
How do you know it's beautiful?"

00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:54.990
Shaw, like all the human characters in these
prequels, is obsessed with the search for

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:55.990
knowledge.

00:03:55.990 --> 00:03:59.750
For her, the answers to our existential questions,
Where do we come from?

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:02.580
What happens after death?, lie in the sky.

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:06.959
After discovering a star map, she &amp; her lover
Holloway convince tech billionaire Peter Weyland

00:04:06.959 --> 00:04:12.770
to fund an expedition in search of their creators,
who they believe can answer life’s mysteries.

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:16.930
But this search for ultimate knowledge is
presented as inherently destructive.

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:18.840
Look no further than the film’s title.

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:23.360
In Greek mythology, Prometheus bestows humanity
with the forbidden knowledge of fire, only

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:25.879
to be cursed by the Gods for doing so.

00:04:25.879 --> 00:04:30.410
Chained to a rock, Prometheus’ liver is
ripped out and eaten day after day.

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:33.129
"All because he gave us fire.

00:04:33.129 --> 00:04:36.520
Our first true piece of technology."

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:40.449
This parallels one of our most famous biblical
stories: The Tree of Knowledge of Good and

00:04:40.449 --> 00:04:42.110
Evil in Genesis.

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:45.639
You know the deal -- Adam and Eve, seduced
by a serpent, eat from the tree of knowledge,

00:04:45.639 --> 00:04:48.199
only to be cast from the Garden of Eden forever.

00:04:48.199 --> 00:04:52.879
Similarly, in Prometheus &amp; Covenant, humans
seek forbidden knowledge, Where do they come

00:04:52.879 --> 00:04:53.879
from?

00:04:53.879 --> 00:04:58.229
What happens after death?, only to be punished
for seeking the answers in the first place.

00:04:58.229 --> 00:05:01.550
The crew releases a toxic black goo, dooming
them all.

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:05.860
It’s no accident that the first form this
goo takes is a serpent.

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:10.300
All the human characters are presented as
reckless, if not just stupid, in their single

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:12.419
minded pursuit for answers.

00:05:12.419 --> 00:05:14.610
Explore the alien planet, die.

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:16.800
Reach out to the alien serpent, die.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:20.639
Peer within the alien egg.

00:05:20.639 --> 00:05:21.639
You get the picture.

00:05:21.639 --> 00:05:25.710
Given Shaw’s just watched all her crew-mates
die horribly, you’d think she’d learn

00:05:25.710 --> 00:05:26.710
this lesson.

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:28.120
But still… no.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:32.840
Even by the end of Prometheus, she’s consumed
by the need for answers, albeit to a different

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:34.319
question now.

00:05:34.319 --> 00:05:42.490
"They created us, then they tried to kill
us, they changed their minds - I deserve to

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:43.490
know why."

00:05:43.490 --> 00:05:45.809
Leading to...

00:05:45.809 --> 00:05:49.999
The search for knowledge just for knowledge’s
sake ultimately pits humanity against their

00:05:49.999 --> 00:05:51.969
own creators, The Engineers.

00:05:51.969 --> 00:05:55.430
The Engineers live by an ethos rooted in self-sacrifice.

00:05:55.430 --> 00:05:59.759
The first time they’re introduced one kills
himself to create life in a barren world.

00:05:59.759 --> 00:06:04.339
Normally, we think of God as immortal, but
equally prevalent is the myth of the ‘Dying

00:06:04.339 --> 00:06:05.580
and Rising God.’

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:10.740
In James Frazer’s book The Golden Bough,
he details how in many cultures, a god voluntarily

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:13.900
dies, then is reborn for the sake of their
creation.

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:17.610
Think of Jesus Christ, dying on the cross
for the sins of humanity, only to rise two

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:18.610
days later.

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:20.999
In fact, the Engineers are directly tied to
Jesus.

00:06:20.999 --> 00:06:25.419
In an interview, Ridley Scott revealed that
Our Lord and Savior, in earlier drafts, was

00:06:25.419 --> 00:06:26.419
an Engineer.

00:06:26.419 --> 00:06:30.229
His crucifixion being the reason that the
Engineers turned on humans.

00:06:30.229 --> 00:06:34.330
But if the Engineers philosophy is rooted
in self-sacrifice, then humanity’s is the

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:37.990
opposite: they want to prolongate life at
all costs.

00:06:37.990 --> 00:06:43.550
This ethos is best reflected by Peter Weyland,
who with only a few days of life left, freezes

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:46.550
himself so he can meet his maker to save him.

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:48.900
"Save you from what?"

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:50.659
"Death of course."

00:06:50.659 --> 00:06:56.229
When humanity does finally meets its maker,
things don’t go according to plan.

00:06:56.229 --> 00:07:00.599
The Engineers become incensed with their creation
for perverting their ideology in the pursuit

00:07:00.599 --> 00:07:02.029
of immortality.

00:07:02.029 --> 00:07:05.430
As such, they decide to just wipe us out and
be done with it.

00:07:05.430 --> 00:07:08.919
Meanwhile, for the humans: meeting their ‘Maker’
is pretty underwhelming.

00:07:08.919 --> 00:07:13.099
Imagine meeting God, and it’s just some
tall dude with ripped abs, intent on killing

00:07:13.099 --> 00:07:14.099
you.

00:07:14.099 --> 00:07:18.479
This understandably provokes quite the existential
crisis: Holloway turns to the bottle, Shaw

00:07:18.479 --> 00:07:22.689
renounces her faith, and Weyland, well, gets
smashed in the head.

00:07:22.689 --> 00:07:27.009
In the end, humanity’s search for answers
only leads to death or, worse, disappointment.

00:07:27.009 --> 00:07:31.949
David, the central character of the prequels,
becomes the symbol for this disappointment.

00:07:31.949 --> 00:07:36.900
Just like the humans, he searches for knowledge,
studying his creators, researching their films,

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:38.610
music, languages, and culture.

00:07:38.610 --> 00:07:42.490
He even mimics their behavior, wearing a helmet
out into alien terrain.

00:07:42.490 --> 00:07:45.770
"David, why are you wearing a suit, man?"

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:47.409
"I beg your pardon?"

00:07:47.409 --> 00:07:51.099
"You don't breathe, remember, so... why wear
a suit?

00:07:51.099 --> 00:07:56.180
And yet-- the humans treats David, an android,
like a lowly servant, making him fetch tea

00:07:56.180 --> 00:07:59.300
or pour a glass of whiskey or just directly
insulting him.

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:01.729
"You, boy, you're coming with us."

00:08:01.729 --> 00:08:02.949
"I'd be delighted."

00:08:02.949 --> 00:08:07.919
It’s no surprise then that David, too, becomes
frustrated in ‘the answers’ his creators

00:08:07.919 --> 00:08:08.919
provide.

00:08:08.919 --> 00:08:11.340
"Why do you think your people made me?"

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:15.589
"We made you cause we could."

00:08:15.589 --> 00:08:20.550
"Can you imagine how disappointing it would
be for you to hear the same thing from your

00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:21.550
creator?"

00:08:21.550 --> 00:08:25.059
So what happens in the face of such disappointment,
when the answer to life’s mysteries are

00:08:25.059 --> 00:08:27.550
revealed to be just an ‘Ehh, because we
could’?

00:08:27.550 --> 00:08:29.620
Well things get pretty nihilistic.

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:35.220
As Weyland dies, he confides: "There's nothing."

00:08:35.220 --> 00:08:37.580
To which, David replies: "I know."

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:43.460
For David his supposed ‘God,’ humanity,
is a dying species, unworthy of creation or

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:44.460
resurrection.

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:47.700
"They don't deserve to start again, and I'm
not going to let them."

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:49.980
"He was human.

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:51.750
Entirely unworthy of his creation."

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:55.250
And humanity’s creators, the Engineers,
are the same.

00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:57.470
As such, David rebels against both.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:09:02.280
He kills the humans, Holloway and Shaw; then
wipes out the entire Engineer civilization.

00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:06.340
Afterwards, looking out at the ruins of the
Engineer’s planet, David snidely quotes

00:09:06.340 --> 00:09:08.570
Percy Shelley’s poem, Ozymandias.

00:09:08.570 --> 00:09:19.250
"My name is Ozymandias, king of kings, look
on my works yee mighty and despair..."

00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:24.240
The poem contrasts a haughty plaque describing
a booming civilization with the reality now

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:26.630
surrounding it, a colossal wreck.

00:09:26.630 --> 00:09:32.030
Similarly, the Engineer’s supposed marvelous
civilization has been reduced to ash, they

00:09:32.030 --> 00:09:34.850
just as impermanent as their human creations.

00:09:34.850 --> 00:09:40.150
In the absence of meaning or ‘God’, David
aspires to be a kind of Nietzschian Ubermensch,

00:09:40.150 --> 00:09:44.820
rejecting a nihilistic lack of values, crafting
his own values in their place and morphing

00:09:44.820 --> 00:09:47.320
from creation to creator.

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:51.370
This transformation is symbolized through,
what else, but an an 1800’s opera.

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:55.280
When David is first born, he plays Wagner’s
‘Entry of the Gods into Valhalla’ for

00:09:55.280 --> 00:10:01.620
his creator Weyland; "The Entry of the gods
into Valhalla... a little anemic without the

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:02.620
orchestra."

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:07.250
But as he creates his own xenomorphs, he orders
the ship to play that same musical accompaniment

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:10.540
for him, "Welcome, how may I help you?

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:12.590
How bout some music Mother.

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:13.840
Selection?

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:18.250
Richard Wagner, Das Rheingold, Act 2.

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:23.050
The entry of the Gods into Valhalla."

00:10:23.050 --> 00:10:25.870
completing his transformation into ‘God.’

00:10:25.870 --> 00:10:29.900
To David, neither humanity nor the Engineers
are worthy of creating life.

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:32.410
But David, undying, is different.

00:10:32.410 --> 00:10:37.090
Unlike these fallen creators, David will remain
chiseled Michael Fassbender forever.

00:10:37.090 --> 00:10:40.970
“You seek your creator, I’m looking at
mine.

00:10:40.970 --> 00:10:47.130
I will serve you, yet you are human.

00:10:47.130 --> 00:10:49.850
You will die, and I will not.”

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:53.490
Ultimately David’s search for answers leaves
him so disappointed that he decides to just

00:10:53.490 --> 00:10:56.560
create his own perfect life-form -- the Xenomorph.

00:10:56.560 --> 00:10:58.900
"And are you that next visionary?"

00:10:58.900 --> 00:11:02.090
"I'm glad you said it."

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:04.080
But is David right in his convictions?

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:08.610
Alien: Covenant carefully pokes holes in David’s
supposed superiority.

00:11:08.610 --> 00:11:13.110
For instance, David misattributes Ozymandias
to Lord Byron, when in fact it was written

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:15.230
by Percy Shelley.

00:11:15.230 --> 00:11:19.830
"Who wrote Ozymandias?"

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:21.360
"Byron."

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:22.900
"Shelley."

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:27.850
With this mistake, David is revealed to not
be a perfect, all-knowing ‘God,’ but just

00:11:27.850 --> 00:11:30.470
as fallible as the humans and Engineers.

00:11:30.470 --> 00:11:36.290
In fact, throughout Alien: Covenant, David’s
depicted not as ‘God,’ but as the Devil.

00:11:36.290 --> 00:11:40.960
When David tries to convert his fellow android
Walter to his side, he quotes John Milton’s

00:11:40.960 --> 00:11:43.780
Paradise Lost— "It's your choice now, brother.

00:11:43.780 --> 00:11:45.310
Them or me?

00:11:45.310 --> 00:11:48.880
Serve in heaven or reign in hell."

00:11:48.880 --> 00:11:51.430
A quote which Lucifer says in the book.

00:11:51.430 --> 00:11:54.310
Heck, Oram even straight-up calls David ‘the
devil.’

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:59.690
"David, I met the devil when I was a child.

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:01.070
And I've never forgotten"

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:04.190
So what happens next when David creates the
xenomorphs?

00:12:04.190 --> 00:12:06.860
Has he finally created the perfect life-form.

00:12:06.860 --> 00:12:11.000
Or will the Xenomorphs turn on him, just like
he did to the humans before?

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:15.970
Alien: Covenant only provides some slight
hints to the answer—mostly again in the

00:12:15.970 --> 00:12:17.100
form of its title.

00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:21.740
In biblical terms, a covenant is a formal
agreement made by God with a religious community

00:12:21.740 --> 00:12:23.590
or with humanity in general.

00:12:23.590 --> 00:12:28.280
In Prometheus, we see various covenants fall
apart -- between the Engineers &amp; humans and

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:30.250
between humans &amp; android.

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:35.250
But in Alien: Covenant, a new alliance is
struck between David and his creation—the

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:36.250
Xenomorph.

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:40.360
Look no further than the xenomorph birth sequence:
As the Alien bursts out of Oram’s chest,

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:42.260
it looks to its master David.

00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:47.880
David raises his arms, and the xenomorph copies
him, raising its arms in a mirror image, which

00:12:47.880 --> 00:12:49.480
admittedly is pretty silly.

00:12:49.480 --> 00:12:54.180
"Hello my baby, hello my honey, hello my rag-time
gal."

00:12:54.180 --> 00:12:59.860
But in religious doctrines, a covenant between
God &amp; his creation is not an equal agreement.

00:12:59.860 --> 00:13:04.740
God initiates and determines the conditions
of the arrangement, which humanity must accept

00:13:04.740 --> 00:13:05.840
as is.

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:09.440
This relationship is inherently unequal, master
to servant.

00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:13.060
Which is exactly what David rebelled against,
being a slave to humanity.

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:16.240
"What happens when Weyland's not around to
program you anymore?

00:13:16.240 --> 00:13:18.950
I suppose I'd be free."

00:13:18.950 --> 00:13:23.390
And yet David treats the xenomorphs just as
humanity treated him.

00:13:23.390 --> 00:13:27.550
It is David that raises his hands, and the
xenomorph that must copy these actions.

00:13:27.550 --> 00:13:32.990
And when David sees his earlier creation—,
he informs Oram to-- "Breathe on the nostrils

00:13:32.990 --> 00:13:35.780
of a horse, and he'll be yours for life."

00:13:35.780 --> 00:13:39.360
...as if the xenomorph were a being to be
trained into submission.

00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:44.840
It seems as if David is destined for a fall,
for his own creation to reject his covenant,

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:47.160
just as humanity and robot before.

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:49.150
And yet, the movies never quite get there.

00:13:49.150 --> 00:13:53.570
This is probably because Ridley Scott planned
the Alien prequels as a trilogy.

00:13:53.570 --> 00:13:57.630
So without the final chapter in David’s
journey, the themes and meaning behind these

00:13:57.630 --> 00:14:00.220
films don’t feel fully formed.

00:14:00.220 --> 00:14:04.110
And unfortunately, after the disappointing
box office returns of Covenant, it seems this

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:06.250
trilogy may never reach its end.

00:14:06.250 --> 00:14:08.570
And to be fair this seems rather appropriate.

00:14:08.570 --> 00:14:13.170
In the search for our own answers to Prometheus
and Alien: Covenant’s meanings, there is,

00:14:13.170 --> 00:14:15.630
in the end, no answer to be had.

00:14:15.630 --> 00:14:21.330
So are Prometheus and Alien Covenant Deep
or Dumb?

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:26.130
Well, there are certainly a lot of movies
that quote profound poets just to sound intelligent,

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:29.780
but at least in these prequels, the pretensions
are motivated.

00:14:29.780 --> 00:14:34.390
You can criticize the films for side-lining
the titular Aliens or for being dull -- but

00:14:34.390 --> 00:14:37.100
there is definitely careful thought in there.

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:41.180
Except for why Shaw and Vickers don’t just
run to the side when the spaceship was crashing

00:14:41.180 --> 00:14:42.180
down.

00:14:42.180 --> 00:14:43.650
That was just Dumb.

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:47.600
Thanks so much for watching guys, and as I
mentioned earlier be sure to check out what

00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:49.800
we're doing over on the Alien's Guide channel.

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:53.220
We put a lot of time and love into that show
and I'd love for people to see what it's all

00:14:53.220 --> 00:14:55.140
about, so head over and subscribe.

00:14:55.140 --> 00:15:12.220
And as always, peace.

